import Proofs.HadwigerNelson.Instances.Heule510.Edges

/-!
# `heule510` — geometry for edges 0–357

Each line below says: these fifty listed pairs really are one unit apart. Generated by
`tools/emit_cert.py` and **not trusted** — the kernel re-derives every one of them from
exact integers, so wrong coordinates cannot pass.

## If one of these fails

The kernel will tell you *which chunk* and not which edge. To get the edge:

```lean
#eval heule510.badEdges     -- every offending pair, and the squared distance it has
#eval heule510.denomSq      -- the squared distance a real unit edge must show
```

`badEdges` runs compiled, so it is instant at any size, and an empty result is exactly
a valid certificate (`UDCert.badEdges_eq_nil_iff`).
-/

namespace HadwigerNelson

theorem heule510Chunk000_valid : heule510.ValidOn heule510Chunk000 = true := by decide +kernel
theorem heule510Chunk001_valid : heule510.ValidOn heule510Chunk001 = true := by decide +kernel

end HadwigerNelson
